In a video game there is a board divided into squares, with $27$ rows and $27$ columns. The squares are painted black, gray and white as follows:
• in the first row, the first square is black, the next is gray, the next is white, the next is black, and so on;
• in the second row, the first is white, the next is black, the next is gray, the next is white, and so on;
• in the third row, the order is gray, white, black, gray, and so on;
• the fourth row is painted the same as the first, the fifth the same as the second, the sixth the same as the third, and so on.
The square in row $i$ and column $j$ contains $ij$ coins; for example, the square in row $15$ and column $20$ contains $15\cdot 20 = 300$ coins. Verify that the black squares contain in total $9^2 (13^2 + 14^2 + 15^2)$ coins.

Shikaku and his son Shikamaru must climb a staircase that has $2022$ steps, numbered $1, 2, \ldots, 2022$; the floor is considered step $0$. They tie a rope between them so that they can be separated by at most $7$ steps, that is, if they are on the steps $m$ and $n$, then $|m-n| \le 7$ must always hold. They play a game with the following rules:
a) they move alternately;
b) in his turn, a player must move to a step higher than the one he was on before;
c) if a player has just moved to the $n$-th step, then on the next turn the other player cannot move to any of the steps $n-1$, $n$ or $n + 1$, except to reach the last step;
d) whoever reaches the last step (step $2022$) wins.
Both start on the floor, and the father moves first. Determine which of the two players has a winning strategy and describe it.
